<!--
    Right-toggle icon while the widget's SPORT view is showing (NEW 18/09/2026, Yann: "En vue
    sport, sur la droite, remplacer les flèches par un bouton cloche et flèches qui tourne. Même
    comportement.") — the existing rotating-arrows glyph (ic_widget_switch_view) with a small
    notification-bell badge in the bottom-end corner, same badge-over-glyph composition already
    used for the app-icon badge on a generic "Toutes notifs" tile (widget_notif_N_badge, 14dp over
    a 32dp image) — a dark circular backdrop first so the white bell reads clearly against the
    white arrows underneath it. Purely static (no runtime bitmap needed, unlike the Sofascore
    variant below), so it's just assigned via RemoteViews.setImageViewResource — see
    NowBarWidgetProvider.applyRightToggleIcon.

    The behavior stays exactly what the plain arrows icon already did (toggleSportAllNotifs) —
    only the SPORT-view icon changes, to indicate where tapping it leads (the "Toutes notifs"
    view). See NowBarWidgetProvider.sofascoreToggleIconBitmap for the symmetric ALL_NOTIFS-view
    icon (a real, runtime-derived white silhouette of Sofascore's own icon — never a hand-drawn
    recreation of it, since that's a real app's own logo).
-->
<layer-list xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">
    <item android:drawable="@drawable/ic_widget_switch_view" />
    <item
        android:width="13dp"
        android:height="13dp"
        android:gravity="bottom|end">
        <shape android:shape="oval">
            <solid android:color="#CC1A2230" />
        </shape>
    </item>
    <item
        android:width="10dp"
        android:height="10dp"
        android:gravity="bottom|end"
        android:drawable="@drawable/ic_notification_bell" />
</layer-list>
